statement:
A string of parentheses counts as **valid** in exactly these cases:

- it is empty;
- it is two valid strings placed one after the other;
- it is a valid string with one `(` added at its start and one `)` added at its end.

You are given `s`, made only of `(` and `)`. A move inserts one parenthesis, of either kind, at any position you choose (the ends included). Return the smallest number of moves after which `s` is valid.

validator:
function validate([s]) {
  if (typeof s !== 'string' || s.length < 1 || s.length > 1000) return 's needs 1 to 1000 characters.';
  if (!/^[()]*$/.test(s)) return "s may contain only '(' and ')'.";
  return null;
}

